ber for Climate Change and Environment","date":"30/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Strategic Budget Report - Public Health 2026-2027","url":"https://Bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s13071/strategic-budget-report-public-health-2026-2027.pdf","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Health and Wellbeing","date":"10/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Personal Budgets Flexible Purchasing System - Re-procurement of Lot 2 Brokerage Award","url":"https://Bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s13023/personal-budgets-flexible-purchasing-system-re-procurement-o.pdf","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Adults and Community Housing Services","date":"06/03/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Adults and Community Housing Services","time":"12.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Children's Services","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Culture","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member Leaders Portfolio","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member Deputy Leaders Portfolio","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Stronger Communities","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member Climate Change, Environmental Services and Regulatory Services","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member for Health and Wellbeing","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive Cabinet Member Highways, Transport, Planning and Development","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"No significant governance issues identified for 2025-26, despite identified improvement opportunities in audit resources, risk management, and procurement.","lead":"A positive assurance position on governance frameworks provides confidence in the council's control environment. This is relevant context for a lender assessing whether identified improvement areas represent governance breakdown or normal continuous\u2026","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Audit assessment found gaps in Procurement Act compliance; consistency of commissioning practice across council needs improvement.","lead":"Procurement governance gaps represent financial control risk and may indicate inconsistent value-for-money assurance across the council's spending, a core concern for both finance directors and lenders.","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Audit found information governance oversight needs strengthening; Business Improvement Review underway.","lead":"Weak information governance oversight creates data security and regulatory compliance risks that could expose the council to operational disruption and reputational damage, both concerns for lenders assessing resilience.","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","headline":"No significant governance issues identified for 2025-26, despite identified improvement opportunities in audit resources, risk management, and procurement.","detail":"The council's review of governance effectiveness has not identified any significant governance issues to report for the year ended March 2026. The council notes it continues to monitor and respond to a range of wider risks including significant financial challenges, changes in service demand, inflation, supply chain risks, workforce capacity, and new legislation.","category":"governance","matters":"A positive assurance position on governance frameworks provides confidence in the council's control environment. This is relevant context for a lender assessing whether identified improvement areas represent governance breakdown or normal continuous improvement.","figures":"Not specified in the paper","quote":"The review process has not identified any significant governance issues necessary to highlight in this statement but there are challenges and opportunities that may impact on future ways of working and governance arrangements that continue to be reflected in the AGS Development Plan.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","headline":"Audit assessment found gaps in Procurement Act compliance; consistency of commissioning practice across council needs improvement.","detail":"An audit assessment of Procurement Act compliance identified that while some areas show strong commissioning and procurement practice, there is a need for greater assurance over the consistency of approach across all council activities. An improvement plan will be delivered in 2026-27, informed by a follow-up internal audit review, with the initial assessment reporting by December 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"Procurement governance gaps represent financial control risk and may indicate inconsistent value-for-money assurance across the council's spending, a core concern for both finance directors and lenders.","figures":"Not specified in the paper","quote":"An audit assessment of compliance with the Procurement Act and management's own review of arrangements conformed that there are further steps that could be taken to ensure visibility and governance of procurement activity across the Council.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","headline":"Audit found information governance oversight needs strengthening; Business Improvement Review underway.","detail":"Internal Audit and management reviews identified opportunities to strengthen oversight of information governance arrangements across the council and to ensure directorate engagement in information governance standards and compliance. A Business Improvement Review is underway to assess approach and structures, reporting by December 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"Weak information governance oversight creates data security and regulatory compliance risks that could expose the council to operational disruption and reputational damage, both concerns for lenders assessing resilience.","figures":"Not specified in the paper","quote":"Internal Audit and management reviews have confirmed opportunities to strengthen the oversight of information governance arrangements across the Council to both strengthen corporate functions and ensure engagement of directorates and departments in information governance standards and compliance","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","headline":"Risk management framework inconsistently applied at strategic and directorate level, and not regularly updated.","detail":"The council identified that its risk management strategy and framework for reviewing strategic and directorate-level risks has been inconsistent and outdated. A new Risk Management Strategy has been agreed by the Corporate Leadership Team and Audit Committee, with risks now managed via SharePoint and integrated into dashboards. However, the regularity of review needs to be embedded over a full year cycle before effectiveness is confirmed.","category":"governance","matters":"Inconsistent and outdated risk management reduces the council's structured visibility of emerging risks to service delivery and financial stability, which a lender would expect to be actively managed.","figures":"Not specified in the paper","quote":"Risk management strategy and framework for review of risks at strategic and directorate level is inconsistent and has not been updated on a regular basis.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-2026","paper_url":"https://bolton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s16738/16738.pdf","headline":"Internal Audit resources significantly reduced, limiting delivery of the planned annual audit programme.","detail":"Internal audit capacity has experienced significant reductions in staffing. This has constrained the council's ability to deliver its full annual audit plan as reported to the Audit Committee. A resourcing strategy is being developed to address the shortfall, including exploring shared resources from other councils and options to strengthen the service, with proposals to be shared by end September 2026.","category":"audit","matters":"Reduced audit capacity weakens the council's ability to provide assurance over financial controls and governance. A lender assessing the control environment needs to know whether internal audit has sufficient resources to identify control weaknesses.","figures":"Not specified in the paper","quote":"Internal Audit resources are reduced significantly and this has limited the ability to deliver the annual audit plan as reported to Audit Committee.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-19"},"name":"Bolton","findings_total":52,"news_drafts_total":3}}